===============================================================================

PgPeek has been installed and mounted at /pg_peek.

Next steps:

1. Map your databases to their ActiveRecord classes in
   config/initializers/pg_peek.rb:

     config.connections = { "primary" => "ApplicationRecord" }

   Every database you want to inspect needs an entry, or it will not be listed.

2. Visit /pg_peek to view your PostgreSQL databases

Before deploying:

   PgPeek has no authentication of its own. Anyone who can reach the route can
   read your schema, every normalized query in the database, and reset query
   statistics. Mount it behind whatever authentication your application already
   uses, for example:

     authenticate :user, ->(user) { user.admin? } do
       mount PgPeek::Engine, at: "/pg_peek"
     end

===============================================================================
